{
  "analysis": "The binary runs successfully with `node vm.js`! It prints stdout appropriately - Doom initializes, finds doom.wad, and starts loading. However, it terminates early at PC=0x1b4d8 after only 4.6M instructions, likely hitting an unimplemented instruction or an error. The message \"R_InitSprites: Sprite TROO : A : 1 has two lumps mapped to it\" is the last output before termination. I need to check what instruction is at that PC and what's causing the termination. The early termination could be due to an unimplemented MIPS instruction, a division by zero, or a TEQ trap.",
  "plan": "Check what's at PC=0x1b4d8 in the binary to understand why it terminated. Also check if /tmp/frame.bmp was created. The issue might be an unimplemented instruction like MULT (not MUL), or a trap instruction.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null || echo \"No frame file\"</arg_value><arg_key>duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-objdump -d /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -B2 -A2 '1b4d8:'</arg_value><arg_key>duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-addr2line -e /app/doomgeneric_mips -f 0x1b4d8</arg_value><arg_key>duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
